 R←Test_UC_054(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;folder;res;tempDir;msg;rc;stop;ref
⍝ Add a Tatin package to "dependencies" and another one to "dependencies_dev", both without a target namespace.
⍝ Adding the second one with loading must re-load the first one as well, because both go into the project space.
⍝ The test for the build list file of the other folder lacked a "/", so the first package used to vanish.
⍝ *** WARNING: want to rename this fn? Keep in mind to rename its folder under "Tests/" as well:
⍝ ***          the test data is located via this function's own name (∆GetTestPath⊃⎕SI).
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '∘∘∘ ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 #.⎕SHADOW'TEMP' ⋄ 'TEMP'#.⎕NS''
 folder←∆GetTestPath⊃⎕SI
 tempDir←∆GetFolderInTempDir⊃⎕SI
 tempDir ⎕NCOPY⍠1⊢folder,'/*'

 ref←∆GetRefToCommTools
 ref.AddAutomation'YesOrNo' 'ChangeCurrentDir@' 'n'
 stop←0
 (rc msg res)←stop ∆UCMD'OpenProject ',tempDir,' -projectSpace=TEMP -batch -ignoreUserExec'
 Assert rc=0

 ref.AddAutomation'YesOrNo' 'AddTatinDeps@' 'y'
 ref.AddAutomation'YesOrNo' 'LoadTatinDependenciesAfterAdding@' 'y'
 (rc msg res)←stop ∆UCMD'AddTatinDependencies [tatin]FilesAndDirs ',tempDir
 Assert rc=0
 →T.GoToTidyUp 9≠#.TEMP.⎕NC'FilesAndDirs'

 (rc msg res)←stop ∆UCMD'AddTatinDependencies [tatin]Tester2 ',tempDir,' -development'
 Assert rc=0
 →T.GoToTidyUp 9≠#.TEMP.⎕NC'Tester2'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 9≠#.TEMP.⎕NC'FilesAndDirs'

 ref.AddAutomation'YesOrNo' 'ClearWS@' 'n'
 (rc msg res)←∆UCMD'CloseProject ',tempDir,' -fast'
 Assert rc=0

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 ref.Cleanup
 res←∆LINK'Break' '#.TEMP'
 FilesAndDirs.RmDir tempDir,'/..'
⍝Done
